011.steps:
1) Configure a new interface X2 , zone: LAN/DMZ/WAN¡
2) Edit this interface in IPv6 interface page, select the ip-assignment as DHCPv6, enable PD, connect it to a DHCPv6 server, make sure it can acquire PD from this server, e.g. the acquired PD length is 48;
3) Configure a LAN interface X3, switch to Advanced tab, click the "add address" button;
4) Click the radio button"Add Downstream IPv6 Address Delegated from DHCP-PD" , choose one of DHCPv6 delegated prefix from the drop-down list(e.g. X2 delegated prefix), then set the preferred IPv6 address, set the preferred prefix length:e.g. 64. and if X2 PD length is 50, and the preferred prefix length is 48 , and finally , the X3 IPv6 address's prefix length will be 50

